(5403535, 774133, 6783, '<td valign="top">This deserved a ribbon. Even with the sky a little too bright is a wonderful shot. I gave you a 9, since you were able to capture the essence of the challenge without a constructed studio photo.<br/>I often notice that the votes and comments focus on the technicality rather than the ideas.<br/>Well thinked and done.</td>', 'This deserved a ribbon. Even with the sky a little too bright is a wonderful shot. I gave you a 9, since you were able to capture the essence of the challenge without a constructed studio photo.I often notice that the votes and comments focus on the technicality rather than the ideas.Well thinked and done.', '2009-03-27 07:27:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(5403589, 773013, 101531, '<td valign="top">The discolouration of Superman is caused by the glow of the laser, like it is being so pronounced on his head/face. It was overall the colour of his legs.<br/>I''m being hurt again on another challenge on this DNMC thing. Lesson learned! Stick to the obvious because some people don''t seem to put much effort in understanding the connection of some pictures to a challenge topic. There is no wonder there are a lot of pictures of the same thing during challenges. People are afraid to step out and use imagination. So, I''ll be doing the same thing from now on. Thanks for the support. <br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by rinac:</b></div><hr/><i> Wow, those scores are a bit rough, eh?<br/> <br/>I realised pretty much straight away that it was a cut-out. Not hard to tell given the odd discolouration. With this in mind, it was easier for me to let go of doggedly trying to work out where the light was coming from, and enjoy what you had done with the laser. Guess others weren''t as relaxed about it.<br/> <br/>The laser is not just the main light source, it''s the <b>only</b> light source AND the main subject. Which means, Superman is rightfully the main subject as well, since <b>HE IS</b> the source of light, duh. The whole "not the main subject" issue, is really a bit over the top and I suspect bandied about by those who want to justify their vote.<br/> <br/>Sheesh people, just chill and enjoy the fun stuff for a change... </i></td></tr></table></td>', 'The discolouration of Superman is caused by the glow of the laser, like it is being so pronounced on his head/face. It was overall the colour of his legs.I''m being hurt again on another challenge on this DNMC thing. Lesson learned! Stick to the obvious because some people don''t seem to put much effort in understanding the connection of some pictures to a challenge topic. There is no wonder there are a lot of pictures of the same thing during challenges. People are afraid to step out and use imagination. So, I''ll be doing the same thing from now on. Thanks for the support.  Originally posted by rinac: Wow, those scores are a bit rough, eh? I realised pretty much straight away that it was a cut-out. Not hard to tell given the odd discolouration. With this in mind, it was easier for me to let go of doggedly trying to work out where the light was coming from, and enjoy what you had done with the laser. Guess others weren''t as relaxed about it. The laser is not just the main light source, it''s the only light source AND the main subject. Which means, Superman is rightfully the main subject as well, since HE IS the source of light, duh. The whole "not the main subject" issue, is really a bit over the top and I suspect bandied about by those who want to justify their vote. Sheesh people, just chill and enjoy the fun stuff for a change... ', '2009-03-27 08:21:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(5403628, 774161, 81530, '<td valign="top">Great shot. 7 from me.</td>', 'Great shot. 7 from me.', '2009-03-27 08:39:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(5403831, 773198, 66515, '<td valign="top">Great abstract and I am confused why it wouldn''t have scored higher. I am guessing that it might be the abstract nature of the image but still: Its an interesting and engaging image.</td>', 'Great abstract and I am confused why it wouldn''t have scored higher. I am guessing that it might be the abstract nature of the image but still: Its an interesting and engaging image.', '2009-03-27 11:36:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(5403841, 774161, 70128, '<td valign="top">I have a question, see if anyone can answer. WHO IN THE WORLD rated this picture with a 2? It must have been either a blind or an envious person. Geez people, come on now! Be real!<br/> <br/>Irene, your shots are always marvelous, and I admire your perseverance. You try and try and try until you get the perfect shot. You are a perfectionist, and I love that! <br/> <br/>CONGRATULATIONS!</td>', 'I have a question, see if anyone can answer. WHO IN THE WORLD rated this picture with a 2? It must have been either a blind or an envious person. Geez people, come on now! Be real! Irene, your shots are always marvelous, and I admire your perseverance. You try and try and try until you get the perfect shot. You are a perfectionist, and I love that!  CONGRATULATIONS!', '2009-03-27 11:46:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(5404061, 774252, 47470, '<td valign="top">If someone wants to be mean, they could have SC disqualify this image because of the wrong date.  Change the date of your camera NOW so you won''t have problems later!</td>', 'If someone wants to be mean, they could have SC disqualify this image because of the wrong date.  Change the date of your camera NOW so you won''t have problems later!', '2009-03-27 16:28:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(5404101, 773013, 45475, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by cup4tml:</b></div><hr/><i> The discolouration of Superman is caused by the glow of the laser, like it is being so pronounced on his head/face. It was overall the colour of his legs.</i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Ah, I see now! Thanks for that :)<br/> <br/>And don''t let the nay-sayers stifle your creativity or growth!</td>', 'Originally posted by cup4tml: The discolouration of Superman is caused by the glow of the laser, like it is being so pronounced on his head/face. It was overall the colour of his legs.  Ah, I see now! Thanks for that :) And don''t let the nay-sayers stifle your creativity or growth!', '2009-03-27 17:21:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(5404741, 774252, 86895, '<td valign="top">Again, the title is very fitting!  I''m very captivated by this shot.  I really want to know what''s going on in the darkness.  Your images are very interesting and thought provoking.</td>', 'Again, the title is very fitting!  I''m very captivated by this shot.  I really want to know what''s going on in the darkness.  Your images are very interesting and thought provoking.', '2009-03-28 02:17:43.000000', NULL, 0),
