(5419241, 773302, 16106, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by jdannels:</b></div><hr/><i> needs more micro-tweaking. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thats exactly what I thought, you so smart.<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by photobytes:</b></div><hr/><i>How long did it take before the bulb burst, with all the heat.</i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>About 45 seconds of burn time<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Titia:</b></div><hr/><i>It''s a lamp alright, but as far as I can see it''s not your light source.</i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Not really clear what this means. Do you mean that the lamp ought to have been lit, and that the fire is a second element? or do you mean the highlights thrown by the secondary lamp used to bring out the treads? The blue flame is about 85% of the light in the image, so while there is a secondary source visible it isn''t the main source, and I''m not willing to work with flame in the dark even for DPC.<br/> <br/><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2009-04-05 03:14:30.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by jdannels: needs more micro-tweaking.   Thats exactly what I thought, you so smart. Originally posted by photobytes:How long did it take before the bulb burst, with all the heat.  About 45 seconds of burn time Originally posted by Titia:It''s a lamp alright, but as far as I can see it''s not your light source.  Not really clear what this means. Do you mean that the lamp ought to have been lit, and that the fire is a second element? or do you mean the highlights thrown by the secondary lamp used to bring out the treads? The blue flame is about 85% of the light in the image, so while there is a secondary source visible it isn''t the main source, and I''m not willing to work with flame in the dark even for DPC. ', '2009-04-05 03:49:12.000000', '2009-04-05 04:14:30.000000', 0),
